{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/17/codegen_prompts/7.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed581286445/17`\n- 题号：`7`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/17/7.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"7\">\n- `description`：根据每行彩色方块的排列顺序构建\"堆叠指令\"，将底部模板图案逐层着色后堆叠输出。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 网格分为上下两个区域，由一条水平 grey 分隔线隔开。\n  - 下方区域包含一个由 grey 像素绘制的小型模板图案（如 3×3 的 L 形或 T 形），位于区域中央。\n  - 上方区域包含若干行\"指令行\"，每行由 1 到 4 个彩色像素从左到右排列（颜色如 red、blue、green、orange 等），不同行的像素数量可以不同。指令行之间用空行（纯 black 行）分隔。指令行从上到下依次编号为第 1 行、第 2 行等。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 指令行的数量决定输出中模板图案被复制的次数。\n  - 输出网格中，将模板图案复制 N 次（N = 指令行数量），从下到上堆叠排列，每层之间无间隙（紧密贴合，下一层的顶行紧接上一层的底行上方）。\n  - 第 k 层（从底部数起第 k 层，k=1 为最底层）使用第 k 行指令行的第一个颜色来绘制模板图案。\n  - 每行指令行中的像素数量表示该层图案需要向右偏移的像素数：若指令行有 M 个像素，则该层图案相对于最底层的位置向右偏移 M-1 个像素。\n  - 输出网格的宽度和高度自动调整以容纳所有堆叠的图案。背景为 black。\n\n- `Key insight`：指令行同时编码了两种信息——第一个像素的颜色决定对应层的着色，而像素的总数量决定该层的水平偏移量。解题者需要识别出同一行指令中\"颜色\"和\"计数\"分别控制不同的变换维度，而非简单地将指令行逐像素映射。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/b1986d4b, eval/3e6067c3, train/20fb2937, train/e3fe1151, train/d749d46f, eval/dbff022c, train/42f83767, eval/9385bd28\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b1986d4b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3564\nmechanism=0.4620\nlexical=0.0113\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:square, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/b1986d4b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/b1986d4b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRender the filled-square object counts as compact nested stacks ordered by count rank.\n\nInput structure\nA large noisy grid has a dominant background, scattered non-square noise, and\nfilled monochrome square objects. Each square side length has exactly one\nobject color, and side lengths form consecutive sizes.\n\nRule\nIgnore non-square components. If the lowest square in the scene is of the\nsmallest side length, treat that one smallest square as a distractor and do\nnot count it. For count rank k from left to right, create one block from all\nsquare sizes with at least k remaining objects; draw larger squares first and\nsmaller squares over their upper-left corner, then append one background\nseparator column.\n\nKey insight\nThe output is a count histogram of square side lengths, but each histogram\nslot is rendered as nested upper-left square masks using the side colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"filled monochrome square objects s, grouped by side length after ignoring non-square noise and the lowest square when it is smallest\",\n  \"dst\": \"left-to-right count-rank stack slots d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"a side group s contributes to slot d_k iff count(s) >= k\",\n  \"transform\": \"draw each slot as nested upper-left square masks, larger sides first; append one bg separator column after every slot\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height is largest side + 1; width is sum of slot widths plus one separator per slot\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"3e6067c3\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3355\nmechanism=0.3722\nlexical=0.0118\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:square, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:aligned, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/3e6067c3.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/3e6067c3.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nConnect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.\n- Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.\n\nRule:\n- Start at the square matching first control color c0.\n- For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.\n- Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.\n\nKey insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"adjacent pixel pair s in a sequence of control pixels in bottom area\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"keep src\",\n  \"dst\": \"merge with adjacent square pair d in an array of squares with colored inner square in main area\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.colors == d.inner_squares.colors\",\n  \"transform\": \"connect d.inner_squares with s[0].color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"process control pairs from left to right\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"control pixels indicates connection path\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"20fb2937\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3279\nmechanism=0.4282\nlexical=0.0123\ncode_feature=0.2857\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:square, object:template, operation:count, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/20fb2937.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/20fb2937.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace each marker below the separator with the mapped top legend square centered on that marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background surrounds a top legend, one solid non-background separator row, and a lower marker field.\n- The legend contains equal-size filled square sprites, with a singleton marker below each sprite and aligned to its center column.\n- The lower field contains only background and marker colors from the legend.\n\nRule:\n- Pair legend markers to legend sprites by left-to-right position.\n- Discard the legend and separator; keep the grid width and the rows below the separator.\n- In the lower field, replace every marker pixel by a filled square of the paired sprite color, centered at the marker location.\n\nKey insight: The top area is a positional color legend, and the actual output is the post-separator marker field expanded by that legend.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"filled square sprite s in the top legend\",\n  \"dst\": \"lower marker d as center anchor\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.color == singleton marker color below s\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"top legend maps each singleton marker color to its filled square sprite\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"rows below the separator, same width\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e3fe1151\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2748\nmechanism=0.3416\nlexical=0.0125\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:counter, object:axis, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e3fe1151.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e3fe1151.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill the one blank in each corner region so all four regions have the same color multiset.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant background color forms one solid separator row and one solid\n  separator column.\n- The separator cross splits the grid into four equal rectangular corner regions.\n- Each corner region contains exactly one background-colored blank pixel.\n\nRule:\n- Count the non-background colors in each corner region.\n- The completed region multiset is defined by the maximum observed count of\n  each color across the four regions.\n- Replace each region's blank pixel with the single color needed to match that\n  completed multiset.\n\nKey insight:\n- The separator color inside a corner region is a missing value marker; comparing\n  the four regions reveals the shared multiset without using numeric color order.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"four equal corner regions divided by a solid background cross, each with one background-colored blank pixel\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill each blank with the color needed so every corner region has the same color multiset, using the maximum observed count of each color across the regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d749d46f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3295\nmechanism=0.4222\nlexical=0.0119\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:aligned, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d749d46f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d749d46f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPack each solid foreground rectangle twice: wide across the top and tall from the bottom.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one background color and one foreground color; the foreground forms\nseparate solid rectangles, ordered from left to right.\n\nRule\nBuild a 10-row background canvas whose width is the packed width of the wide\nversions of the rectangles. For each source rectangle, paint a top-aligned\nrectangle of shape min(h,w) by max(h,w), with one background column between\nconsecutive rectangles. Then, starting again from the left edge, paint a\nbottom-aligned rectangle of shape max(h,w) by min(h,w) for each source rectangle,\nagain separated by one background column.\n\nKey insight\nThe input rectangles are not copied in their original orientations; each object\ncontributes one horizontal-facing and one vertical-facing normalized rectangle,\npreserving left-to-right object order.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"solid monochromatic foreground rectangles ordered left-to-right\",\n  \"dst\": \"packed upper wide slots and lower tall slots in the same left-to-right order\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"rank(s) == rank(d) for both the upper and lower slot sequences\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint each rectangle twice: min(h,w) by max(h,w) top-aligned in the upper band, and max(h,w) by min(h,w) bottom-aligned in the lower band, with one background column between slots\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height 10; width is the sum of max(h,w) over source rectangles plus one separator column between consecutive rectangles\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
